  "body": "Stacked on #2054 (branch `mkinney:issue/2018-weldon-per-taper`, with `main` merged in for #2029). Merge #2054 first; this diff then shows only the #2016 commits. Fork synced from upstream `main` at c86d6db35.\n\n## What changed\n\nA tool that sits in a built-in library holder stores a reference to the entry, not a drawn copy of its outline.\n\n- `camcraft_tools::holder_library::HolderRef {entry, gauge_len, projection}` (new, `crates/tools/src/holder_library_ref.rs`), carried on `ToolBody::library`.\n- `tool_body::build_library` is the one place a reference becomes a shape. `SetToolBody::library`, `AddTool` (stated and machine-default holder), the project loader and the `.camtools` reader call it. `tool_body::judged`, `stack`, `digest`, the simulation and the preview read the body it returns, as before. The #828 floor for a machine-default holder is unchanged.\n- Files: the tool key `holder: {entry, gauge_len, projection}` (plus `machine_default: true` when assumed) is written in place of `body`. Project v62 (the unreleased step the issue names); a `.camtools` file says version 2 when a tool names a library holder.\n- Migration: an older file is not rewritten. A drawn copy of a library holder stays a custom drawn profile with the same outline, and a `holder_d`/`holder_len` cylinder stays the tool's own numbers.\n- Refusals by tool name: an entry the library does not hold, a grouped pick (\"BT40 Weldon\"), lengths the entry cannot take, a holder that reaches into the flutes, an unknown key in the reference, `holder` beside `body`. No other holder is put in its place.\n- MCP: `set_tool_holder` with `library` writes the reference; the reply and `get_job` show it as `holder.library`. `add_tool` refuses a `holder` reference inside `definition`; `edit_tool` refuses a `holder` patch. Skill rows updated.\n- UI: with a referenced holder the tool settings show the holder diameter and length the laws read as text, not as two fields. The Profile tab names the entry and the picker shows it. The unchanged outline applied again keeps the reference; one edited point makes the holder a custom profile (one undo step).\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/2016-holder-reference.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green on the final head (tools, app and ui suites), and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. macOS (m5).\n\nPinning tests:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/holder_reference.rs`\n  - `every_entry_reads_the_same_bands_by_reference_as_its_old_copy`: for every library entry, at the default and at other lengths, picked and assumed: the judged tool, envelope, band stack, stamp term and facets equal those of the drawn copy an older build stored, also after a save and load.\n  - `an_older_project_loads_as_custom_holders_with_the_same_collision_result`: a v61 project with a drawn copy and a plain holder cylinder loads with the same reads, operation status and warnings (the BT30 flange strikes the fixture wall, hit for hit).\n  - `an_older_tool_library_loads_as_custom_holders_and_a_new_one_round_trips_the_reference`\n  - `an_unknown_entry_refuses_the_file_by_name_and_never_lands_another_holder` (project and `.camtools`)\n  - `a_library_holder_is_the_reference_in_the_document_and_the_file`\n  - `the_unchanged_outline_keeps_the_reference_and_an_edited_point_makes_it_custom`\n  - `mcp_set_tool_holder_writes_the_reference`\n- `crates/tools/src/holder_library_ref.rs` unit tests.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_holder_reference.rs`: `a_library_holder_sizes_the_holder_fields_until_its_outline_is_edited`, `the_profile_tab_names_the_entry_and_the_picker_shows_it`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Windows and Linux. The release tier and the pixel-snapshot lanes (no snapshot PNG changed).\n- No real v0.21.0 file was read: the older file in the tests is this build's file rewritten to the older form (`body` with the drawn copy, version 61 / 1).\n- The app was not driven by hand.\n\n## Notes for the reviewer\n\n- A build of main between #1453 and this change reads v62 and would drop the `holder` key (development builds only; v0.21.0 refuses v62).\n- A corrected library entry now reaches every project that names it. A copy kept the old numbers.\n- The tool record's `holder_d`/`holder_len` are not overwritten by the entry (they are what the tool goes back to when the holder is cleared, and writing them would move the stamp). The settings show the entry's numbers.\n\nChangelog: A tool's library holder is stored as a reference to the library entry (name, gauge length, projection) in the project and tool library files, not as a drawn copy; the tool settings show the entry's holder size. Breaking: v0.21.0 and older refuse a file that names a library holder.\n\nEffort: max (no escalation)\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: a project or tool library saved with a library holder states it as a reference (project v62, `.camtools` version 2); v0.21.0 and older refuse such a file.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nFixes #2016\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n## UI screenshots\n\nThese images show the seeded `EM-0600-4FL` tool with the `BT30 ER20` holder.\nThe gauge length is 60 mm. The projection is 55 mm.\n\nThe egui test harness drives the production shell and renders these PNGs with the GPU renderer.\nThe before captures use the four UI and profile-state source files from `e661ece1`.\nThe backend stays at `822c4c9a` to supply the same holder geometry in both captures.\nThe after captures use the current head, `822c4c9a`.\n\n### Holder size controls\n\nBefore: the holder diameter and length are editable fields.\n\n![Holder size controls before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/ba10296eb7199e2b37254900e26f188302e5a1c8/2092/holder-controls-before.png)\n\nAfter: the controls show the library holder diameter and length, with the entry name.\n\n![Holder size controls after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/ba10296eb7199e2b37254900e26f188302e5a1c8/2092/holder-controls-after.png)\n\n### Profile tab\n\nBefore: the tab identifies a drawn profile. The library picker has no selection.\n\n![Holder Profile tab before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/ba10296eb7199e2b37254900e26f188302e5a1c8/2092/holder-profile-before.png)\n\nAfter: the tab names the library holder. The picker shows `BT30 ER20`, the gauge length, and the projection.\n\n![Holder Profile tab after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/ba10296eb7199e2b37254900e26f188302e5a1c8/2092/holder-profile-after.png)\n",
